# Villain Codex - magic items
SOURCELONG:Villain Codex	SOURCESHORT:VC	SOURCEDATE:2017-11

Badge of Authority	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:1500	WT:0.5	SOURCEPAGE:p.44	SPROP:As a standard action, the wielder can transform its appearance into that of any badge or symbol of authority she legitimately holds. Once per day, she can present the badge as a standard action to reduce the base speed of up to three creatures within 30 feet, as per hobble (Fortitude DC 11 negates). If the wielder uses Intimidate to force a creature to act friendly and that creature recognizes her as a legitimate authority, its attitude doesn't change to unfriendly after 1d6x10 minutes, and it doesn't report her to local authorities.	DESC:This solid metal badge lets its wielder impersonate authority and cow onlookers. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, cause fear, silent image; Cost 750 gp.
Erasing Book	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:400	WT:3	SOURCEPAGE:p.45	SPROP:Once per day as a standard action, the holder can erase the non-material-component writing contained within this leather-bound book. It can be used as a spellbook or formula book; spells written in it with a material component cost are immune to the erasing effect. Erasing also removes smudges, stains, and minor water damage, but does not recover text lost to serious damage.	DESC:An erasing book. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, erase; Cost 200 gp.
Pliability Elixir	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Potion	COST:500	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.45	SPROP:A creature that drinks this elixir becomes mentally and emotionally pliable for 10 minutes (Will DC 16 negates). Bluff, Diplomacy, and Intimidate checks automatically succeed against a pliable creature, except Diplomacy checks to improve its attitude (normal DC). After 1 minute the effect is noticeable with a DC 25 Sense Motive check. A vial appears to be an elixir of truth unless identified by 10 or more.	DESC:Pliability elixir. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, charm person, zone of truth; Cost 250 gp.
Quill of Verification	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:1000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.45	SPROP:This swan-feather quill verifies signatures. Store a signature by pressing the quill into it and speaking a command word, then tap another signature to check authenticity as if attaining a 20 on a Linguistics check; the quill glows blue if legitimate. It can validate a signature up to 3 times per day, and the stored signature can be switched any number of times between uses.	DESC:Quill of verification. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, identify; Cost 500 gp.

Ankle Chains of Walking	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:6000	WT:5	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:Locked around a helpless or willing creature's ankles as a full-round action, the creature can move only half its normal speed for all forms of movement. The creator can remove them with a command word; any creature with a DC 30 Disable Device check; the restrained creature with a DC 30 Escape Artist check. Dispelling suppresses but does not remove them.	DESC:Steel cuffs joined by a 2-foot chain, inlaid with lead broken-feet motifs. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, slow; Cost 3,000 gp.
Branding Iron of Tracking	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:9000	WT:5	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:When its sigil is heated in fire, this 2-foot metal rod brands a creature or object. Afterward, anyone holding the iron knows the direction to the nearest brand, as locate object for branded objects or locate creature for branded creatures. It tracks only the brand itself, so cutting or scraping off the brand fools the item.	DESC:A metal rod tipped with a unique sigil. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, brand (APG), locate creature, locate object; Cost 4,500 gp.
Darkness Arrow	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:80	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:This +1 arrow infuses magical darkness into a struck creature's sight: it counts the light level as darkness for 1 round regardless of actual light, and a creature with darkvision must succeed at a DC 13 Fortitude save or lose its darkvision for 1 round.	DESC:A jet-black arrow fletched with raven feathers. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, darkness; Cost 40 gp.
Gag of Silence	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:500	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:When tied around a creature's head with the wooden ball in its mouth, the creature cannot speak or make vocal sounds, including verbal spell components. Removing it breaks the ball off the cord, ending the effect. An unrestrained creature can easily untie and remove the gag.	DESC:A black leather cord with a red wooden ball at its center. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, silence; Cost 250 gp.
Sleeping Sap	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:10301	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:On a confirmed critical hit, this +1 sap puts a creature to sleep for 3 minutes as per sleep, with no HD limit (Fortitude DC 13 negates).	DESC:A magically enhanced leather sap. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, sleep; Cost 5,301 gp.
Vine Arrow	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:80	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.21	SPROP:When this +1 arrow strikes a foe, vines grow from the creature's body. Any creature within 5 feet of the struck target, including the target, is entangled for 1 round unless it succeeds at a DC 13 Reflex save.	DESC:An arrow that looks like a plant stem fletched with leaves. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, entangle; Cost 40 gp.
Aerialist's Rod	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Rod	COST:3200	WT:5	SOURCEPAGE:p.32	SPROP:Three studs activate different modes. Balancing Pole: extends to 7 feet, grants a +5 competence bonus on Acrobatics and a +3 enhancement bonus on Reflex saves (both only for maintaining balance, held in both hands), and acts as a masterwork quarterstaff. Tightrope: anchors a horizontal rope up to 100 feet. Trapeze: anchors two ropes to a ceiling up to 40 feet up for swinging across gaps.	DESC:A well-worn 2-foot brass rod capped with a metal loop at each end. Construction Requirements: Craft Rod, animate rope, cat's grace; Cost 1,600 gp.
Fool's Malady	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Ring	COST:900	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.33	SPROP:When worn, the ring causes the wearer to develop a single fixed deformity over 1 minute (set when forged, unchangeable). It modifies rather than replaces appearance, so acquaintances still recognize her. If the wearer already has the mimicked deformity, the ring instead removes all visual traces of it (but not associated pain or penalties).	DESC:A simple lead ring carved with a twisting face. Construction Requirements: Forge Ring, alter self; Cost 450 gp.
Home Away	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:18000	WT:600	SOURCEPAGE:p.33	SPROP:A horse-drawn caravan wagon whose owner can change its coloration and patterns or unfold one wall into a stage by command word. The always warm and dry interior houses foldaway furniture for up to six Medium creatures. Once per week the owner can pull the kingbolt to unfurl it into a 60-foot-wide tent furnished for a declared purpose.	DESC:A wooden-walled caravan wagon. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, major creation, silent image, tiny hut; Cost 9,000 gp.
Mountebank's Megaphone	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:4500	WT:3	SOURCEPAGE:p.33	SPROP:Held in one hand, this cone makes the holder's voice up to 10 times louder. A holder with bardic performance can treat any space within a 30-foot cone in front of him as the origin of a performance that normally centers on the performer, at double the usual round cost; moving ends the projected performance.	DESC:A garishly painted cone of brass hoops and leather. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, ghost sound, exquisite accompaniment; Cost 2,250 gp.
Powerhouse Pelt	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:3515	WT:20	SOURCEPAGE:p.33	SPROP:This +1 hide armor grants a +2 competence bonus on all ability checks to perform feats of strength (bending bars, forcing doors), but not on other Strength rolls. The wearer also treats her Strength as 8 higher for determining carrying capacity.	DESC:Hide armor crafted from a great cat's skin. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, ant haul (APG), bull's strength; Cost 1,915 gp.
Mage Shot (Acid)	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:178	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.57	SPROP:This +1 alchemical paper cartridge changes a firearm's damage to acid. A target that takes acid damage from it takes an additional 2d4 acid damage for the next 2 rounds or until neutralized; this does not stack with multiple shots or with acid arrow.	DESC:An alchemical paper cartridge (dragoon versions cost triple). Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, acid arrow; Cost 98 gp.
Mage Shot (Cold)	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:178	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.57	SPROP:This +1 alchemical paper cartridge changes a firearm's damage to cold. A target that takes cold damage from it must succeed at a DC 14 Fortitude save or be staggered for 1d4 rounds.	DESC:An alchemical paper cartridge (dragoon versions cost triple). Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, cone of cold; Cost 98 gp.
Mage Shot (Electricity)	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:178	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.57	SPROP:This +1 alchemical paper cartridge changes a firearm's damage to electricity. A target that takes electricity damage from it must succeed at a DC 14 Fortitude save or be dazed for 1 round.	DESC:An alchemical paper cartridge (dragoon versions cost triple). Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, lightning bolt; Cost 98 gp.
Mage Shot (Fire)	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:178	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.57	SPROP:This +1 alchemical paper cartridge changes a firearm's damage to fire. A target that takes fire damage from it must succeed at a DC 14 Reflex save or catch on fire, taking an additional 1d6 fire damage each round until the flames are extinguished.	DESC:An alchemical paper cartridge (dragoon versions cost triple). Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, scorching ray; Cost 98 gp.
Plagueborn Mantle	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Cloak	COST:7200	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	SPROP:Functions as a +1 cloak of resistance. If the wearer is diseased, he can command it to cast virulent miasma once per day. Also, a diseased wearer can make a standard-action touch attack; on a hit the target must succeed at a DC 15 Fortitude save or contract one disease the wearer currently has (wearer's choice).	DESC:A cloak sewn from the preserved skins of plague victims. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, contagion, resistance, virulent miasma; Cost 3,600 gp.
Reaper's Lantern	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:9515	WT:10	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	SPROP:This +1 heavy flail sheds light as a hooded lantern (adjustable to a 5-foot dim radius). Once per day on a hit the wielder can deal an extra 2d6 negative energy damage as a swift action, gaining that many temporary hp for 1 hour. A creature dropped to 0 or fewer hp by it must succeed at a DC 13 Fortitude save or die (death effect); the flame then holds an echo of that soul for 24 hours for speak with dead.	DESC:A black iron lantern-and-chain flail burning with cold blue-green flame. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, continual flame, death knell, speak with dead, vampiric touch; Cost 4,915 gp.
Urgathoa's Breath	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2500	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	SPROP:A thrown weapon (10-foot range increment) that shatters on impact, releasing a 10-foot cloud of mist as fog cloud for 1 round. Any creature that enters the mist must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or contract a fast-acting bubonic plague strain with immediate onset.	DESC:A smoked-glass sphere of roiling bone-white mist. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, contagion, fog cloud; Cost 1,250 gp.
Balor's Lash	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:10301	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.81	SPROP:This +1 flaming whip deals extra damage whenever used for a non-damaging combat maneuver such as trip or drag: once the maneuver resolves, the target (or an object it moved, as via disarm) takes 2d6 fire damage.	DESC:A whip marked with a red flame motif. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, Whip Mastery, fireball; Cost 5,301 gp.
Ivory Succubus	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:5000	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.81	SPROP:A statue that emits a constant magic aura to seem nonmagical. An owner attunes it through 24 hours of revelry costing at least 500 gp and can reshape its provocative pose. While any other creature possesses it, that creature must succeed at a DC 11 Will save each day or shift one attitude step toward helpful regarding the attuned owner; failing enough saves makes it helpful until it loses the statue.	DESC:A 6-inch ivory statue of a succubus that seems to shift pose daily. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, charm person, magic aura; Cost 2,500 gp.
Devil's Spit	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:60	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.92	SPROP:A more potent unholy water. A direct hit deals 4d4 damage to good outsiders and lawful good creatures, 6d4 to lawful good outsiders, and 2d4 to other good creatures; splash deals 1-3 points by category. A vial can instead charge a rod of burning blood with 5 charges (a standard action that provokes).	DESC:A vial of caustic blessed-in-reverse fluid. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, curse water; Cost 30 gp.
Diabolus Bell	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:16000	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.93	SPROP:Once per day, ringing the bell (standard action) lets lawful Asmodeus worshippers within 20 feet pray as a move action to gain ward the faithful. Chaotic or good hearers must succeed at a DC 13 Will save or be affected as doom; chaotic good creatures that fail also take 1d8 sonic damage and must save (DC 13 Fortitude) or be stunned 1 round. Living creatures at -1 or fewer hp must save (DC 13 Will) or be slain as death knell.	DESC:A black iron bell inscribed with diabolical symbols. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, death knell, doom, sound burst, ward the faithful; Cost 8,000 gp.
Eyes of Embersight	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:16000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.93	SPROP:On command (a prayer to Asmodeus, standard action), the wearer gains 60-foot darkvision that pierces darkness of any kind, including deeper darkness. Active lenses glow like red-hot embers, foiling Disguise unless disguised with glowing red eyes. Works 9 minutes per day in 1-minute increments; both lenses must be worn by the same wearer.	DESC:Two transparent red crystal lenses worn over the eyes. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, true seeing; Cost 8,000 gp.
Eyes of the Damned	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:15000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.93	SPROP:On command (a prayer to Asmodeus, standard action) the wearer gains a gaze attack until her next turn and may target one creature within 30 feet: it must succeed at a DC 14 Will save or be affected as vision of Hell for 5 minutes (a following phantasm). Devils and lawful evil creatures are immune. Usable three times per day; both lenses must be worn by the same wearer.	DESC:Two clear crystal lenses worn over the eyes. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, vision of Hell; Cost 7,500 gp.
Rod of Burning Blood	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:11050	WT:4	SOURCEPAGE:p.93	SPROP:A +1 cunning light mace. Unholy water poured over it is absorbed as 1 charge per vial (max 10). On a hit the wielder may spend 1 charge to spray burning blood for 1d6 damage (half fire, half unholy), or spend 5 charges for a 15-foot cone dealing 5d4 damage (half fire, half unholy; Reflex DC 17 half). A vial of devil's spit provides 5 charges.	DESC:A blackened iron rod inset with rubies. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, Craft Rod, flame strike, true strike; Cost 5,525 gp.
Crate of Preservation	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2500	WT:60	SOURCEPAGE:p.117	SPROP:Stores up to 8 cubic feet of perishable food and drink and keeps it fresh indefinitely; cold items stay cold and hot items stay hot. Food already spoiled before being placed inside is not restored and simply remains in its current state.	DESC:A sturdy crate that preserves its contents. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, endure elements, purify food and drink; Cost 1,250 gp.
Unbalanced Scales	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:1000	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.117	SPROP:Normally gives accurate weight readings, but by command word the user can make the scales read up to 25% lighter or heavier as desired, letting an unscrupulous merchant cheat transactions while still passing official inspections.	DESC:A merchant's balance scale with a hidden flaw. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, prestidigitation; Cost 500 gp.
Arrow of Latching	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:500	WT:0.1	SOURCEPAGE:p.128	SPROP:Its wrapping is 100 feet of hemp rope shrunk to 1/16 size. Fired at a Medium or larger object, it embeds if the roll hits AC 5 + the object's hardness. Anyone within 200 feet can command the rope to unfurl to full size and hang down 100 feet; a command-speaker within 100 feet with a free hand has it swing into his hand. The rope bears up to 1,000 pounds. Removing the arrow reduces it to a common arrow.	DESC:An arrow seemingly wrapped in twine. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, animate rope, handy grapnel, shrink item; Cost 250 gp.
Hood's Flair	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2500	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.129	SPROP:A token tied to a ranged or thrown weapon (full-round action) grants one use per day of its power (extra uses cost 1 grit or panache each); only one token works at a time. Black Feather: a 5-foot step gains 5 extra feet. Brass Leaf: allies do not give cover against her ranged attacks until end of turn. Silver Chime: reroll a ranged miss chance from concealment. Teal Bead: a ranged attack does not provoke.	DESC:A garish token adorning a weapon. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, haste, creator must be able to use grit or panache; Cost 1,250 gp.
Hook of Ascension	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:12500	WT:0.5	SOURCEPAGE:p.129	SPROP:Attached to a rope or cable, the user moves along it 30 feet per move action regardless of slope, even straight up, with no Climb checks required, and this movement is not vigorous motion for casting. It can be commanded to stop mid-travel, holding its user suspended along the rope without falling.	DESC:A mithral zip-line hook on a spider-buckled strap. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, levitate, spider climb; Cost 6,500 gp.
Vagrant's Hood	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:4400	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.129	SPROP:Casts a dramatic shadow obscuring the wearer's face and makes her voice sound deep and throaty as vocal alteration.	BONUS:SKILL|Disguise|4	DESC:A linen hood in forest colors. Grants a +4 competence bonus on Disguise checks. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, disguise self, vocal alteration; Cost 2,200 gp.
Fungal Slippers	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2000	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.141	SPROP:As a swift action up to three times per day, the wearer sprouts fungi in every square she walks through that turn, making them difficult terrain. After 1 minute most of the fungi vanish and any that remain no longer impede movement.	DESC:Slippers that seed fungal growth. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, entangle; Cost 1,000 gp.
Necklace of Stolen Breath	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Amulet	COST:3500	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.141	SPROP:A string of carved bones holding drowned souls. The wearer can mimic the voice of any stored spirit (sound mimicry) and can destroy a bone as a standard action to summon a drowned shade (a water elemental with undead traits and a 20-foot drowning aura). Soul bone tiers summon Small to Huge shades or instead heal 1d8+11 to 7d8+11 hp; once per day, dropping below 0 hp she may destroy a bone to heal herself. Price excludes the bones.	DESC:An intricately carved bone necklace. Construction Requirements: Augment Summoning, Craft Wondrous Item, summon monster VI or summon nature's ally V; Cost 1,750 gp.
Ring of Rulership	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Ring	COST:14000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.153	SPROP:As a rod of rulership, but the wearer commands the fealty of citizens or vassals of her own bloodline's holdings. On command she targets one qualifying humanoid within 50 feet; it obeys automatically if Intelligence 9 or lower, otherwise a DC 14 Will save negates (and grants 24-hour immunity). This mind-affecting compulsion counts as a 3rd-level spell for break enchantment. It can rule at most three creatures at a time.	DESC:A garish signet ring worth 1,500 gp in materials alone. Construction Requirements: Forge Ring, mass suggestion; Cost 7,750 gp.
Commander's Tent	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:9000	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.165	SPROP:Planting the miniature flag and speaking a command word expands it into a 15-by-30-foot military tent with table, chairs, lanterns, and a light-proofed vestibule; the exterior does not glow so long as only one vestibule flap is open. Once per week a second command word turns the central blank map into a sand table model of the nearby area. Further command words swap the tent's flag or collapse it back to flag form.	DESC:A small 2-by-3-inch flag on a wooden dowel. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, rope trick, sand table; Cost 4,500 gp.
Moss Cloak	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Cloak	COST:18700	WT:5	SOURCEPAGE:p.165	SPROP:Worn in forest or jungle terrain, it grants a +10 competence bonus on Stealth checks. In any terrain, once per day as a standard action the wearer can remove one poison currently affecting him; doing so turns the moss brown and negates the Stealth bonus until the cloak heals itself 24 hours later.	DESC:A heavy cloak of green moss grown on damp sod. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, invisibility, neutralize poison, restoration; Cost 9,350 gp.
Satchel of Plentiful Feed	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2000	WT:15	SOURCEPAGE:p.165	SPROP:A mesh bag stuffed with hay that produces enough fresh feed each day for a number of mounts by type: Type I (15 lbs, 2,000 gp) feeds 4; Type II (20 lbs, 4,000 gp) feeds 10; Type III (25 lbs, 7,500 gp) feeds 25; Type IV (30 lbs, 15,000 gp) feeds 50. Stats shown are for Type I.	DESC:An overflowing mesh feed bag. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, create food and water; Cost varies (Type I 1,000 gp; Type II 2,000 gp; Type III 3,750 gp; Type IV 7,500 gp).
Battle Strider's Boots	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2000	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.177	SPROP:For the first 24 hours worn they flicker, reducing speed by 5 feet and imposing a -2 penalty on Acrobatics. After that the penalties end and the boots activate: three times per day as a swift action the wearer avoids provoking attacks of opportunity while leaving a threatened square. Creatures with blindsight or true seeing can still make those attacks.	DESC:Rough leather boots that seem to shift position. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, blur; Cost 1,000 gp.
Cutlass of Waves	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:9615	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.189	SPROP:This +1 cutlass is constantly soaked with brine. Its attacks take no underwater penalties, as if it were a piercing weapon. While held, a low-cresting wave of water carries the holder along a ship's deck or through the water as slipstream.	DESC:A brine-soaked cutlass. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, slipstream; Cost 4,650 gp.
Hat of the Seven Winds	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:4500	WT:1	SOURCEPAGE:p.189	SPROP:The wearer takes no penalties from rain, takes high-wind penalties as though one size category larger than she is, and gains a +4 bonus on saving throws against wind effects.	DESC:A black tricorne embroidered with a ship. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, control winds; Cost 2,250 gp.
Pirate Lord's Patch	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:8500	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.189	SPROP:The wearer sees as though the patch were not there. Once per day he can activate see invisibility for 5 minutes, and once per day he can see through solid objects for 1 minute as a ring of x-ray vision.	BONUS:SKILL|Appraise,Intimidate|2	DESC:A gold-cloth eye patch with a sapphire-eyed skull. Grants a +2 competence bonus on Appraise and Intimidate checks. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, locate object, see invisibility; Cost 4,250 gp.
Animal Mask	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:2700	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.201	SPROP:Depicting an ape, bear, boar, cat, fox, horse, pig, rat, or wolf, the mask lets the wearer see through its eyes. As a swift action she can transform her head into that animal for up to 5 minutes per day (in 1-minute increments), absorbing the mask; she keeps normal speech and spellcasting and gains low-light vision, scent, and a bite or gore attack (1d4 Medium, 1d3 Small).	DESC:A mask of cloth and carved bone bearing an animal's parts. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, beast shape I; Cost 1,350 gp.
Society Ring	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Ring	COST:8000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.201	SPROP:Once its wearer is inducted into an organization by a 10-minute ritual, the ring attunes, shows that crest, and becomes invisible and hidden from scrying to all but wearers of similar rings. The wearer can communicate with similar-ring wearers within 150 feet as message and gains a +10 competence bonus on Bluff and Sense Motive checks to pass and receive secret messages among members. Touching two rings links status for 1 hour. Carried by a non-attuned creature, it alerts members within 1 mile as alarm.	DESC:A signet ring set with a semiprecious gem. Construction Requirements: Forge Ring, alarm, hidden speech, invisibility, message, obscure object, status, creator must have 10 ranks in Bluff and Sense Motive; Cost 4,000 gp.
Periapt of Devotion	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Amulet	COST:3300	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.213	SPROP:Presented to a current or prospective member (humanoids only), the recipient must succeed at a DC 11 Will save or be compelled to don it. Thereafter the wearer is devoted to the giver as charm person (no additional save), always viewing her words and actions favorably.	DESC:An amulet bearing a group or cult's symbol. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, beguiling gift, charm person; Cost 1,650 gp.
Periapt of Utter Devotion	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Amulet	COST:33000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.213	SPROP:As a periapt of devotion but with a DC 16 Will save, and it affects nonhumanoids as charm monster. Once per day while talking to the wearer, the giver can implant a triggered suggestion; the wearer may attempt a DC 16 Will save to negate it, and beating the DC by 5 or more also breaks the periapt's charm.	DESC:A potent devotion amulet. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, beguiling gift, charm monster, triggered suggestion; Cost 16,500 gp.
Sigils of the Great Cataclysm	TYPE:Magic.Artifact.Minor	COST:0	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.213	SPROP:A set of seven seals that, buried on the points of a seven-pointed star up to a 3-mile radius, trigger one weekly effect each. First: 10% of living creatures affected by feast of ashes (Will DC 17). Second: 20% by rage (Will DC 18). Third: 30% by contagion (Fortitude DC 19). Fourth: 40% by cloudkill (Fortitude DC 20). Fifth: control weather storms. Sixth: roaming earthquake. Seventh: falling fiery spheres, 2d6 + 1d6 fire each round (Reflex DC 23 half). Moving a seal ends its effect. Destroyed only by submerging a full set in a nixie's pool and casting bless water daily for 1 month.	DESC:Seven seals of stone, clay, or black iron designed to doom a city. Minor artifact; not for sale.
Cestus of Security	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:5305	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.224	SPROP:This +1 cestus can lock a held weapon in place by mental command, granting a +10 bonus to CMD against disarm; while locked the hand cannot make somatic components or skill checks (locking or unlocking is a move action). A leather strap keeps a dropped or disarmed weapon within the wielder's square for recovery as a move action, and a mental command detaches it.	DESC:A blackened leather cestus reinforced with dark iron and spikes. Construction Requirements: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, animate rope; Cost 2,805 gp.
Clandestine Voucher	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:250	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	SPROP:A parchment and magical quill that turn metal coins into dots of metallic ink (one dot per coin; the quill holds 200 coins of one type; the sheet holds 1,600 coins). Applying a solvent restores the coins as mundane coins. Cursed coins cannot be stored. Reuse requires a new 25 gp quill and washing the parchment.	DESC:A parchment for hiding wealth as ink. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, treasure stitching; Cost 125 gp.
Ghungroos of Entrancement	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:3750	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	SPROP:When using a distraction bardic performance the wearer gains a +5 competence bonus on Perform (dance) checks; when using fascinate she gains +1 to the save DC. She may also use Perform (dance) with a countersong performance, gaining a +2 competence bonus on that check.	BONUS:SKILL|Stealth|-2	DESC:Musical anklets strung with tiny bells. The wearer takes a -2 penalty on Stealth checks while wearing them. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, hypnotism, creator must have bardic performance and 5 ranks in Perform (dance); Cost 1,875 gp.
Smoke Bomb of Forgetfulness	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:900	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	SPROP:Thrown as a standard action (at the user's feet or as a ranged touch attack, 20-foot range), it creates a 15-foot-radius smoke cloud like a smokestick. Any creature in the cloud unaware of the bomb's nature must succeed at a DC 16 Will save or have its memory of the previous 2 rounds altered as though its sight had been obscured, forgetting creatures it interacted with. A creature aware of such bombs automatically succeeds.	DESC:A smoke bomb that erases recent memory. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, modify memory; Cost 450 gp.
Vishkanya Periapt	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Amulet	COST:10000	WT:0	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	SPROP:Once per day as a swift action the wearer can envenom a wielded weapon with her saliva or blood as if she were a vishkanya (she may deal 1 point of piercing or slashing damage to herself to use blood). A vishkanya wearer can use her toxic racial trait two additional times per day and increases her venom save DCs by 1.	DESC:A blood-drop ruby on a golden necklace. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, poison; Cost 5,000 gp.
Doorknobs of Peregrination	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:40000	WT:2	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	SPROP:A matched pair of brass doorknobs affixed to two separate solid-surfaced portals within 400 feet. Opening one door opens the other, letting the user and companions step through as if the doors were one; a locked, stuck, or secured door on either side prevents opening. Placing or removing a knob is a standard action; removing the first knob while the door is open extends the portal one extra round.	DESC:Matched brass doorknobs inscribed with spiraling patterns. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, dimension door; Cost 20,000 gp.
Slippers of Scampering	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:1200	WT:0.5	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	SPROP:Function like slippers of spider climbing, except usable for 10 rounds per day, split as the wearer chooses (minimum 1 round per use).	DESC:Light slippers granting brief spider climbing. Construction Requirements: Craft Wondrous Item, spider climb; Cost 600 gp.
